if SHIELD_AIPAD

config ZMK_KEYBOARD_NAME
    default "aipad"

config AIPAD_DISPLAY_SELFTEST
    bool "Draw a boot self test on every ScreenKey"
    default n
    help
      Bring-up aid. Without it, all four ScreenKeys are intentionally dark until
      the host sends an AI client state, which is indistinguishable from broken
      wiring. With it, every screen lights its backlight and draws a logo and a
      full border right after init, independent of the host: even screens show
      the Codex logo in a blue border and odd screens the Claude Code logo in a
      green border, so neighbouring panels are always distinguishable and the
      physical order of CS1..CS4 can be read off the board. A host update still
      takes over normally. Turn this off once the hardware is confirmed.

config AIPAD_ENCODER_PROBE
    bool "Log the live level of the FPC pins the encoder could be on"
    default n
    help
      Bring-up aid for a rotary encoder that does not respond. Every pin on the
      24 way FPC is accounted for by the matrix, the panels or the backlight, so
      the encoder has to be on one of the few pins left over. This samples those
      pins and logs a line whenever one changes: turn the knob and the two that
      toggle together are the encoder, without putting a meter on 0.5 mm pads.
      Build with CONFIG_GPIO_HOGS=n as well, or the hog that parks the WS2812B
      data line holds P0.05 low and hides an encoder channel wired there.

endif
